              "record_type": "finding",
              "status": "poor_practice",
              "title": "Credential in the URL query is written to access logs",
              "summary": "The route reads a credential from the URL query string, and request logging registered before the route records the full URL. Send the credential in the request body (for example with POST) instead of the URL, and keep query strings out of access logs for sensitive routes.",
              "input_validation": "Field validation is reported separately; it does not change what this log line contains.",
              "use_protection": "Logging evidence: request query field current reaches credential evidence \"security.hash(currentPassword) !== loggedInUser.data.password\" and the URL with its query string is recorded by request logging ('combined'); request query field new reaches credential evidence \"password: newPasswordInString\" and the URL with its query string is recorded by request logging ('combined').",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. Semantic assessment was not run. Who can read the log destination and how long it is retained have not been assessed; that does not remove this remediation task.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Keep credentials out of URLs and access logs",
                "actions": [
                  "Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.",
                  "Move the credential from the URL query string to the request body (for example change GET to POST) and update every client that calls the route.",
                  "Until clients change, exclude this route's query string from access logs or use a format without :url for it, and rotate any credentials already written to existing logs.",
                  "Restrict who can read access-log files; a log directory served over HTTP exposes every recorded URL."
                ],
                "illustrative_example": "// Illustrative: accept the credentials in the body, not the URL.\napp.post('/rest/user/change-password', express.json(), (req, res) =\u003e {\n  const { current, new: next, repeat } = req.body;\n  // ...existing checks and update\n});",
                "example_status": "illustrative_template; not a verified application patch"
              }
