              "status": "poor_practice",
              "title": "A value is built into SQL query text",
              "summary": "Refactor the string-built query to keep values separate from SQL structure using the verified driver API. This construction is a poor-practice finding even when an exploitable injection has not been demonstrated. Field validation is a separate concern.",
              "input_validation": "No validator call was identified for the named field in the analyzed handler and modeled middleware. This does not prove that every execution path lacks validation. Evidence: req.query.q reaches a sensitive use with no validator call in the handler or applicable middleware",
              "use_protection": "Not established from the supplied evidence.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. Semantic assessment was not run. Exploitability is separate from the established construction practice; a missing or inconclusive semantic assessment does not remove this remediation task.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Separate input data from SQL structure",
                "actions": [
                  "Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.",
                  "Pass untrusted values through the verified driver's parameter-binding API. Keep SQL query, update, and insert structure separate from data. Review NoSQL APIs separately.",
                  "Restrict each field as far as its business requirement allows. A string or length check is not injection protection. A comment or other free-text field may contain any character, so the sink construction is the injection control.",
                  "Add regression cases for normal input, rejected malformed input and query-structure preservation; resolve inconclusive guard and binding evidence before applying a fix."
                ],
                "illustrative_example": "// Illustrative Sequelize binding pattern; adapt schema and full authentication logic.\nconst rows = await sequelize.query(\n  'SELECT id FROM accounts WHERE email = $email',\n  { bind: { email: req.body.email } }\n);",
