              "record_type": "finding",
              "status": "poor_practice",
              "title": "Untrusted data reaches raw HTML output",
              "summary": "A source-backed input flow reaches a verified rendering sink without established context-appropriate encoding or effective sanitization. Correct the output construction; runtime exploit confirmation is separate.",
              "input_validation": "Input validation is separate from context-appropriate output encoding and sanitization.",
              "use_protection": "Output context: html_text. A verified Angular trust bypass for this context reaches the binding on a source path without modeled sanitization; other paths remain in the evidence.",
              "uncertainty": "Review the evidence for the named claim. Independent findings review and runtime confirmation have not been performed. Semantic assessment was not run. Exploitability is separate from the established construction practice; a missing or inconclusive semantic assessment does not remove this remediation task.",
              "recommendations": {
                "title": "Protect the specific browser rendering context",
                "actions": [
                  "Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.",
                  "Use escaped template output for HTML text and quoted non-active attributes; use textContent for plain DOM text.",
                  "For intentional rich HTML, apply a verified maintained sanitizer before every sink; inspect its configuration and version.",
                  "Treat script, URL, event-handler and unquoted-attribute contexts separately. HTML entity encoding alone does not protect them.",
                  "Preserve source, storage and output links when fixing reflected or stored flows; test the protected counterpart."
                ],
                "example_status": ""
              }
            },
