              "help": {
                "markdown": "Keep credentials out of URLs and access logs\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Move the credential from the URL query string to the request body (for example change GET to POST) and update every client that calls the route.\n- Until clients change, exclude this route's query string from access logs or use a format without :url for it, and rotate any credentials already written to existing logs.\n- Restrict who can read access-log files; a log directory served over HTTP exposes every recorded URL.\n\nIllustrative example (unverified):\n\n```typescript\n// Illustrative: accept the credentials in the body, not the URL.\napp.post('/rest/user/change-password', express.json(), (req, res) =\u003e {\n  const { current, new: next, repeat } = req.body;\n  // ...existing checks and update\n});\n```\n",
                "text": "Keep credentials out of URLs and access logs. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Move the credential from the URL query string to the request body (for example change GET to POST) and update every client that calls the route. Until clients change, exclude this route's query string from access logs or use a format without :url for it, and rotate any credentials already written to existing logs. Restrict who can read access-log files; a log directory served over HTTP exposes every recorded URL."
              },
